#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Managed by Ansible. Read-only diagnostic views for the rpc-ro ACL group.

Called through rpcd "file exec" as `rpc-ro-view <view>`. The ACL pins the exact command
line of every view. The only view that takes arguments is test-routing; its ACL entry is
a pattern, so this script is what validates the arguments (see v_test_routing).

Safety rules for this file:
  * nothing is written anywhere, every external command is run as an argument list
    (never through a shell) with a fixed environment;
  * secrets are masked before they are printed (config views, awg);
  * a view takes no arguments unless it is listed in ARG_VIEWS.
Settings come from /etc/rpc-ro/view.json (rendered by Ansible), DEFAULTS fill the gaps.
"""
